<article class="env-lemma" id="06KY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06KY">Lemma <span data-tag="06KY">90.25.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{F}$ be category cofibered in groupoids over a category $\mathcal{C}$. Let $U : \mathcal{C} \to \textit{Sets}$ be a functor. Let $f : U \to \mathcal{F}$ be a morphism of categories cofibered in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$. Define $R, s, t, c$ as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R : \mathcal{C} \to \textit{Sets}$ is the functor $U \times _{f, \mathcal{F}, f} U$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$t, s : R \to U$ are the first and second projections, respectively. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$c : R \times _{s, U, t} R \to R$ is the morphism given by projection onto the first and last factors of $U \times _{f, \mathcal{F}, f} U \times _{f, \mathcal{F}, f} U$ under the canonical isomorphism $R \times _{s, U, t} R \to U \times _{f, \mathcal{F}, f} U \times _{f, \mathcal{F}, f} U$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $(U, R, s, t, c)$ is a groupoid in functors on $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>